ce=False... wait no: `if change!='scalar' and not scalar_appearance: pick_dirty=True; _selection_index=None`. So appearance generation changes (non-scalar-style) already clear the index directly. The key narrowing is a second-level optimization for the case where the index was NOT cleared — i.e., scalar-only changes: change=='scalar' or scalar_appearance. In those cases generations.scalar (or .appearance) bumped → old key mismatch → rebuild. With narrowed key, rebuild skipped.\n\nNow — improvement 2's cache and improvement 4 interact: the software paint cache signature uses full generations (scalar affects colors) — correct.\n\nNow let me check `_hover_select` GPU path: query_point → for GPU with cached ID target... `_gpu_point_hits` at 1702. GPU hover calls query_point which for GPU uses pick_detail (framebuffer readback). Coalescing at the qt.py level is what improvement 1 wants.\n\nNow let me look at the existing tests to understand the fake-host test harness patterns: tests/test_qt_update_pump.py, test_qt_software_responsiveness.py, test_scheduler.py. These will show how to construct QtViewer fakes without windows. Let me read test_qt_update_pump.py and test_scheduler.py, plus check how test_qt_software_responsiveness builds a fake host for _paint_software.", "summary": []}
